ROADMAP (35 steps)
==================

PHASE A: WEBKIT EXPLOITATION (Browser -> Native Code)
-----------------------------------------------------
1.  Find a WebKit bug (memory corruption - UAF, OOB, type confusion)
2.  Trigger the bug (craft JS/HTML that hits the vulnerable code path)
3.  Stabilize the corruption (heap groom so freed/OOB memory lands predictably)
4.  Get an info leak (read a JSCell/object pointer from corrupted memory)
5.  Defeat ASLR (calculate WebKit heap base from leaked pointer)
6.  Build addrOf primitive (JS object -> its raw heap address)
7.  Build fakeObj primitive (raw address -> treat it as JS object)
8.  Create fake ArrayBuffer (forge a butterfly/backing store pointer you control)
9.  Get arbitrary read (read any userland address via fake ArrayBuffer)
10. Get arbitrary write (write any userland address via fake ArrayBuffer)
11. Defeat WebKit mitigations (Gigacage, StructureID randomization, IsoHeap)
12. Find JIT page or RWX region (or use a code-signing bypass)
13. Write shellcode (place your payload in executable memory)
14. Hijack control flow (overwrite a function pointer or vtable)
15. Execute userland shellcode (native code in WebProcess)

PHASE B: SANDBOX ESCAPE (WebProcess -> Full Userland)
-----------------------------------------------------
16. Escape WebKit sandbox (syscall or IPC escape)

PHASE C: KERNEL EXPLOITATION (Userland -> Ring 0)
-------------------------------------------------
17. Leak kernel ASLR slide (find kernel base address from userland)
18. Find a kernel bug (race condition, UAF, overflow in a syscall)
19. Trigger kernel bug from userland (craft the syscall sequence)
20. Get kernel read primitive
21. Get kernel write primitive

PHASE D: PRIVILEGE ESCALATION (Ring 0 -> Root/Unrestricted)
-----------------------------------------------------------
22. Find kernel credentials struct (locate process ucred)
23. Escalate privileges (uid=0, capabilities/authid)
24. Disable kernel security flags (syscall filtering, sandbox)
25. Disable W^X in kernel (patch PTEs or security policy)
26. Map kernel as RW from userland (or keep kernel R/W primitive)
27. Patch kernel to allow unsigned code

PHASE E: HYPERVISOR BYPASS (Ring 0 -> Ring -1)
----------------------------------------------
28. Defeat hypervisor checks (HV monitors kernel integrity)
29. Find hypervisor bug (separate vuln in the HV layer)
30. Escape hypervisor (HV-level code exec or neutralize monitoring)
31. Disable IOMMU restrictions (DMA to all physical memory)

PHASE F: PERSISTENCE + PAYLOAD (Jailbreak Complete)
----------------------------------------------------
32. Patch secure boot chain
33. Install payload loader (persistent/semi-persistent entry)
34. Load homebrew enabler (HEN/Mira/GoldHEN equivalent)
35. Run unsigned code, dump games, install packages


