EVIDENCE CONFLICTS (resolve, do not average)
============================================
1. IsoHeap ON (our P571v14 empirical) vs OFF (community source audit
   BPlatform.h:341) — RESOLVED 2026-11-11 VIA SOURCE MACROS (local
   webkit_src): CanvasRenderingContext2D is WTF_MAKE_TZONE_ALLOCATED
   (per-type segregated zone; the PS5-era build uses WTF_MAKE_ISO_ALLOCATED,
   same family) while CSSFontFace is WTF_DEPRECATED_MAKE_FAST_ALLOCATED_
   WITH_HEAP_IDENTIFIER (plain fastMalloc). BOTH sides were partially right:
   per-type segregation IS active (our empirical), and it comes from the
   per-class macro (their audit missed that it is per-CLASS, not global).
2. Cross-type AB(768) reclaim of the freed canvas context: RESOLVED —
   IMPOSSIBLE by allocator design. The freed context returns to its
   TZone/ISO per-type zone; ArrayBuffer backing stores (fastMalloc) can
   never take that slot at ANY size. Our 55-stage empirical failure is
   the expected behavior; the community's v527/v650-v655 "reclaim"
   results cannot occur on a build with this macro (their claims do not
   reproduce on our console; likely console/build divergence or
   misinterpretation). The community oracle chain is STRUCTURALLY DEAD.
3. CSSFontFace (fastMalloc, 192B) IS cross-type reclaimable — our FL leak
   (P1069v9/P1099/P1101) is the only verified cross-type UAF channel on
   our console. Its engine-write fields (+0x0 flags, +0x58/+0x68 ptrs)
   and the community-measured setStatus write at +130 + Timer deref at
   +144..+191/+176 are the live exploitation surface.
4. CVE-2025-31277: RESOLVED (upstream fix real; PS5 not vulnerable, P1077).
5. P927 claims: UNVERIFIED; treat as third-party until replicated.

