  4.29GB forward sweep -> WebProcess death (community p141 parity).
- P1162-P1169: code-pointer harvest BLOCKED (10+ runs, zero writes in
  readable memory). P1170/P1171/P1173: CSSFontFace post-free interaction
  = 3-field write only (+0=1, +0x58/+0x68 ptrs); no deref surface.
- P1174: CVE-2026-64783 DEAD (no datalist on PS5). P1175: CVE-2026-65337
  DEAD (fix backported or path absent). P1176-P1178: sort-detach UAF =
  anomaly only, CLOSED as primitive (writes never reach reclaimed memory;
  reads are the sort's own captured data).
- Source-level resolution: CanvasRenderingContext2D = TZONE/ISO per-type
  zone (cross-type reclaim impossible by design); CSSFontFace = fastMalloc
  (reclaimable). Sony selectively backports recent WebKit fixes; live bugs
  are the unpatched-subsystem class (canvas/metadata).
- The "not enough free system memory" system dialog is expected for
  these probes (171MB build + multi-GB sweep); press OK to continue.
